Z||000015||Steve Normington||08-12-2001||12:02 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by hugh:<BR><B>Songman,You could be older,shorter,and poorer like me.Damn,now I need to be cheered up.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>So is this a cheer people up or "my life sucks more than yours" topic?<P>From my own perspective the "it could be worse" usually doesn't help. To the person who is not happy, their problems are what counts, not how much worse things could be. To fierobaby, FieroLisa, and any others who are not happy. Find someone you can trust and unload on them. In person is best, but phone will work as well. It won't solve any of your problems, but it might make them seem a little less painful. I speak from experiance on this, so please think about my advice.<P>Either that or write a country-western song.<P>PS. I thought my live sucked about a year ago, it didn't then and it doesn't now.<P>(((((HUGS)))))||||reg||1
Z||000016||72vinman||08-12-2001||12:04 AM||||You guys are depressing me. Maybe we should all go on a talk show.<BR>Depressed Fiero Owners on the next Opra. <BR>Everytime I get depressed (and trust me those times are more frequent these days) I see someone or read an article about someone that is so much worse off than myself and it helps to bring me back.<BR>Cheer up everyone, life is too short.<P>------------------<BR>72vinman@home.com<BR>Black 86GT||||reg||12
Z||000017||Songman||08-12-2001||12:08 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Steve Normington:<BR><B>Either that or write a country-western song.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Actually, I write country songs every day of my life! hehe That's what I do...<P>And to be honest, I couldn't be much happier. I may not have the perfect life, but I like who I am and that is the main thing anyone should strive for. It took me about 30 years to figure that out...<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||7
Z||000018||72vinman||08-12-2001||12:20 AM||||Hey Songman, I have been writing songs for many years now. Latley When I am depressed and start working on one it ends up with a total country and western feel to it. <BR>Why is that? I am pretty sure that Cowboys are not the only ones that get depressed. Just wondering.<P>------------------<BR>72vinman@home.com<BR>Black 86GT||||reg||5
Z||000019||Cheever2||08-12-2001||12:35 AM||||Let me try...<P><BR>I'm not wearing any underwear.<P><BR>Does that help?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000020||Songman||08-12-2001||12:53 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 72vinman:<BR><B>Hey Songman, I have been writing songs for many years now. Latley When I am depressed and start working on one it ends up with a total country and western feel to it. <BR>Why is that? I am pretty sure that Cowboys are not the only ones that get depressed. Just wondering.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hmmmm.. I have no idea. Country music gets a pretty bad rap from people who don't listen to it and say that it is all so depressing.<P>Some of the things said about country music (by the way, it hasn't been called country & western in years. Country and Western are two different kinds of music now.) are that it is 1)twangy, 2) just three chords, 3) play it backward and you get your truck, dog, wife back, etc...<P>Well, that twang comes from a Fender Telecaster guitar that is used just as much in rock music as country. Just in country the music is not turned up so loud and you can actually hear the guitar... And three chords, well if you know anything about music that is the basic layout for most any song. Actually, some of the biggest hit songs in the world only had two chords, and this is not just for country. And the playing it backwards thing... well, I'll just laugh along with the rest of you because it is a funny joke.<P>Probably the reason your songs end up sounding country when you are depressed is because you put what is in your heart into your songs. And that is what country music is - it is real emotions from real people. It is real life. Of course, when I say this I am talking abour REAL country music. Not that pop crap they are playing on the radio and trying to pass off as country. You'll find very few songs with heart on country radio today. You'll hear a lot of stuff that is so syrupy lovey that it will give you cavities, but it's not real.<P>I spent a lot of years as a staff writer for different publishing companies in Nashville where I would go into town and meet other writers at 10am and sit there and try to crank out songs. I gave that stuff up and moved out to the country and I write songs when an idea hits me now. Songwriting is not a production line kind of thing and that is why we have all these empty songs on the radio now. Those little rooms I mentioned are filled every day by guys hoping to write the next big Faith Hill song and make a million dollars. Personally, I'd rather write a song that will actually touch someone and be remembered 30 years from now.<P>Anyway, obviously this is something that I could talk about for hours and I don't even know if I answered your question. But I can respond to one part of your question... Cowboys? I have no idea. I ride horses but I'm no cowboy. I'm a long-haired, Harley riding, Fiero driving, country music singer.. But I would have to guess that cowboys are not the only ones who get depressed.. <P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000021||Tigger||08-12-2001||12:54 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Steve Normington:<BR><B>Either that or write a country-western song.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Playing a country-western song backwards sometimes cheers me up...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000022||Tigger||08-12-2001||01:00 AM||||Songman, that's what I'm talking about!<P>LOL!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||10
Z||000023||72vinman||08-12-2001||01:05 AM||||Fierobaby and Fierolisa, I find that songwriting can really help to release a whole lot of emotions. I am not suggesting you run out and buy a piano or guitar, but try putting your feelings down on paper. A journal or poetry would work great. <P>Yeah Songman I know what you mean. I have had people that liked my work call me up hoping to make an appointment to write with me. Or have had people give me a deadline to write a song. I can only write what I feel or what I am inspired by and I cannot turn it on like a switch. I do apologize, I did not mean that cowboys are the only ones that listen to country music. I also agree with you about the "new country" It all sounds like pop music to me but I do like it. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>72vinman@home.com<BR>Black 86GT||||reg||7
