Z||000029||AusFiero||08-13-2001||09:58 AM||||God how depressing this has become. I need that like a hole in the head. Dang it, I got one of them already  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||9
Z||000030||Ken Wittlief||08-13-2001||10:29 AM||||Country and Western music?!<P>what ever happened to the western music?<P>the only person I know of in the last 30 years that ever claimed that what he was doing was best described as Western Music was John Denver - all the songs about the rocky mountains and eagles and alaska.<P>If country music has a bad rap its from association with people who live in trailers and drive pickup trunks, wear cowboy boots and wouldnt know how to ride a horse if their life depended on it.<P>Who exactly lives in the country anymore?! not farmers, not cowboys - not in any significant percentage of the population.<P>If some of what John Denver was doing could be considered Western music, living out in the wilderness, living up in the mountains, being independant and free, being in tune with nature and the great open spaces - then maybe a revival of sorts of that kinda music could go somewhere.<P>BTW - if your feeling down strumming away on an old folk guitar and singing some old sad songs is a GREAT way to get over it - a way to express your feelings, get them out, vocalizing your pain, and after a while you really do feel better.||||reg||10
Z||000031||Cheever2||08-13-2001||11:14 AM||||Steve Martin said you can't play a sad song on a banjo.  Maybe more of us should get banjos.<P>(anybody know of a sad banjo song?)<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000032||Songman||08-13-2001||03:56 PM||||Country music has nothing to do with trailers, trucks, horses, cowboy boots, prison, trains, dogs, bar fights, or anything else that people might want to find a reason to look down on it for.<P>And just in case anyone wonders, I don't find any of the things that were mentioned as a reason to give anyone or anything a bad rap. Not every one can afford to live in a big fancy house. I generally find people that live in trailers to be a little nicer and more real. I wear cowboy boots because I want to, of course, most of them are custom made and cost a fortune! I own three pickup trucks and I do ride horses. I have been blessed with good fortune in my life so I can have a choice in where I live or what I drive. But to think that those that haven't are somehow less is just wrong.<P>The point is, while any of these things may be found in country music, they do not make up country music. Country Music is about real people and real lives. It is about music that touches people hearts and lives. Country music is just at home in New York or California as it is in Texas or Tennessee.<P>Now for Western Music... Michael Martin Murphy, Wylie and the Wild West Bunch, Riders In The Sky are three of the first that come to mind. Personally, I considered John Denver more folk than Western.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A><P>[This message has been edited by Songman (edited 08-13-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by Songman (edited 08-13-2001).]||||reg||7
Z||000033||Galen||08-13-2001||04:02 PM||||I was once unhappy, but then I figured  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif">  wtf ya know  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I'll just be happy.. dont worry, be happy hehe||||reg||1
Z||000034||JSocha||08-13-2001||04:54 PM||||&lt;*sniff*, *sniff*, ...bawling...&gt;<P>That was....&lt;crying&gt; that was...&lt;crying harder&gt;...that was so beautiful....<P>&lt;Whaaaaa!&gt; <BR>&lt;Whaaaaaa!&gt;<P>Well, I couldn't find the little crying smiley face to put in here.<P>Cheer up!  You could be me!<P>Sayla vie, Mon Chari!||||reg||9
Z||000035||fierobaby||08-14-2001||11:08 AM||||I wrote a song<P>To the tune of How Forever Feels by Kenny Chesney (I appologize for the first verse I had nothing!)<P>little red Fiero burning in the flames<BR>feet on the pedles couldn't get much hotter<BR>little umbrella shaped smoke clouds<BR>really hot burning valve covers<P>oh now I know how Cliff Pennock feels<P>hands on the wheel crusin' down the interstate<BR>gas pedle sticks carrys my Fiero away<BR>I was going fast as a V-8 goes<BR>I could feel the speed from my head to my toes<BR>oh now I know how V-8 Archie feels<P>I've been around this block a time or two <BR>done almost everything a girl could do<BR>I've done some driving yeah I've had fun<BR>well there is one thing that I haven't done<P>saved two months raced a little honda<BR>tonights the night feels like perfect timing<BR>hit the NOS one on ricers front step<BR>man I'm gonna die if he kicks my a$$<P>I wanna know how a winner feels<P>I've been around this block a time or two <BR>done almost everything a girl could do<BR>I've done some driving yeah I've had fun<BR>well there is one thing that I haven't done<P>I wanna know how a winner feels<BR>hey I wanna know how a winner feels<BR>I wanna know have a winner feels<P>[This message has been edited by fierobaby (edited 08-14-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by fierobaby (edited 08-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000036||Ken Wittlief||08-14-2001||11:17 AM||||Im not raggin on country music or putting it down.<P> when you hear music on the radio you form a mental image of where it might be coming from, a studio, a live concert, a small club... <P>  and you picture who might be playing it, what they look like, what instruments they are using, and you picture who would be in the audience.<P> so I think its fair to say that when most people hear rock music, classical music, country music, german ethnic music... they have a sterotype image of where it came from.<P>  maybe thats unfortunate - maybe its a subtle form of putting people into catigories - but I dont think it can be avoided<P> [BTW I think thats one of the problems with synthisizers, you hear this new sound and your mind draws a blank trying to picture what kinda instrument makes that noise, and in a way you reject it]<P>  I can listen to great music of any style. The problem is when they put on the B side of the record, or the band starts playing some of its 'non-hits' - then I can tolerate some things better than others.<P>  In the end, performing music is an act of courage - having the guts to get up in front of people and in effect, say: "this is how I feel - this is the way I see things - this is what is important to me" in the hope that some of the people listening will identify and connect with what you are revealing about yourself through your music.||||reg||10
